ZERO.BROWSER-CORE / first executable specification

OBJECTIVE
  Produce the smallest real browser core that can later host the ZERO screen reader.
  The core must be independent from speech, braille and network transport.

MODEL
  DOCUMENT
    NODE
      identity
      role
      name
      state
      value
      parent
      children
      relations

  FOCUS
    exactly one active target or NONE
    movement is deterministic
    every movement emits an accessibility event

  EVENT
    kind
    target
    before
    after
    cause
    sequence

  OUTPUT
    semantic event stream is canonical
    speech is a consumer
    braille is a consumer
    logging is a consumer

MINIMUM EVENTS
  DOCUMENT-START
  DOCUMENT-END
  FOCUS-ENTER
  FOCUS-LEAVE
  VALUE-CHANGE
  STATE-CHANGE
  ALERT
  ERROR
  UNKNOWN

MINIMUM ROLES
  DOCUMENT
  HEADING
  PARAGRAPH
  LINK
  BUTTON
  TEXTBOX
  CHECKBOX
  RADIO
  LIST
  LIST-ITEM
  TABLE
  ROW
  CELL
  DIALOG
  ALERT

KEYBOARD
  NEXT
  PREVIOUS
  ACTIVATE
  ESCAPE
  FIRST
  LAST
  BACK
  FORWARD

INVARIANTS
  No pixel/OCR dependency.
  No speech output is parsed to recover semantics.
  No invented label is silently treated as authoritative.
  Unknown state is preserved.
  Every externally visible state transition is observable in the event stream.
  The core remains usable without a speech engine.

VALIDATION
  Feed a deterministic document fixture.
  Replay identical keyboard sequences.
  Require identical semantic event sequences.
  Mutate labels, ordering and nesting independently.
  Verify that navigation follows structure rather than visual coordinates.

NEXT
  Implement this model in an approved non-Python, non-Rust, non-JavaScript host.
  Do not select the host merely for convenience; benchmark accessibility latency,
  semantic coverage and portability first.
